# The builders' context mark, in tokens: the auto-compaction window every builder launches with
# (team-worker's --autocompact, as <tokens/1000>k) and the context at or past which team-next
# gives a fix round to a fresh builder instead of the holder.
# Claude Code compacts a builder about 32k under the window.
# A whole number of tokens of six to nine digits with no leading zero, a multiple of 1000, on the
# one line below that is neither empty nor a comment.
# It is also the context past which team-tokens' report counts a session long.
# Read by bin/lib/context-mark.sh, for team-worker and team-next, and by team-tokens, which reads
# it by the same rule.
tokens=250000
